e wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-jump-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent"><span class="wprm-recipe-icon wprm-recipe-jump-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><g class="nc-icon-wrapper" fill="#ffffff"><path data-color="color-2" d="M9,2h6c0.6,0,1-0.4,1-1s-0.4-1-1-1H9C8.4,0,8,0.4,8,1S8.4,2,9,2z"></path> <path fill="#ffffff" d="M16,11V5c0-0.6-0.4-1-1-1H9C8.4,4,8,4.4,8,5v6H1.9L12,23.6L22.1,11H16z"></path></g></svg></span> Jump to Recipe</a> <a href="https://gingerandscotch.com/wprm_print/homemade-ramen-noodles-from-scratch" style="color: #ffffff;background-color: #e17813;border-color: #333333;border-radius: 10px;padding: 5px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-print wprm-recipe-link wprm-print-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-print-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent" data-recipe-id="15078" data-template="" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><span class="wprm-recipe-icon wprm-recipe-print-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" x="0px" y="0px" width="16px" height="16px" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><g ><path fill="#ffffff" d="M19,5.09V1c0-0.552-0.448-1-1-1H6C5.448,0,5,0.448,5,1v4.09C2.167,5.569,0,8.033,0,11v7c0,0.552,0.448,1,1,1h4v4c0,0.552,0.448,1,1,1h12c0.552,0,1-0.448,1-1v-4h4c0.552,0,1-0.448,1-1v-7C24,8.033,21.833,5.569,19,5.09z M7,2h10v3H7V2z M17,22H7v-9h10V22z M18,10c-0.552,0-1-0.448-1-1c0-0.552,0.448-1,1-1s1,0.448,1,1C19,9.552,18.552,10,18,10z"/></g></svg></span> Print Recipe</a></div><div class="dpsp-post-pinterest-image-hidden" style="display: none;"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%200%200'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-pin-media="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pin-1-Ramen-Noodles.jpg" data-pin-description="How to Make Ramen Noodles From Scratch (the Easy way)rn#homemadenoodlesramen #homemadenoodles #ramennoodles #ramenfromscratch #noodlesfromscratch #kidscooking #kidscookingactivity #alkaline noodles" alt="Learn to make homemade ramen noodles from scratch" class="dpsp-post-pinterest-image-hidden-inner dpsp-post-pinterest-image-hidden-single" loading="lazy" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pin-1-Ramen-Noodles-76x125.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pin-1-Ramen-Noodles-76x125.jpg" data-pin-media="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/Pin-1-Ramen-Noodles.jpg" data-pin-description="How to Make Ramen Noodles From Scratch (the Easy way)rn#homemadenoodlesramen #homemadenoodles #ramennoodles #ramenfromscratch #noodlesfromscratch #kidscooking #kidscookingactivity #alkaline noodles" alt="Learn to make homemade ramen noodles from scratch" class="dpsp-post-pinterest-image-hidden-inner dpsp-post-pinterest-image-hidden-single" loading="lazy" /></noscript></div><span id="dpsp-post-content-markup" data-image-pin-it="true"></span><p class="has-theme-palette-6-color has-theme-palette-8-background-color has-text-color has-background" style="font-size:12px"><em>This post may contain affiliate links where, at no additional cost to you, I receive a small commission when products are purchased through those links. As an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases. Any commisions earned helps keep this site sustainable.</em> <a href="/privacy-and-disclosure-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Click here for privacy policy</a>.</p><p><em>Ramen noodles are easy to make but the dough is tough to knead and roll by hand. To make ramen the easy way, use a pasta machine and let it do all the hard work, essentially making this a no-knead Ramen noodles from scratch method.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="303" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20303'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Chinese Egg Noodles From Scratch" class="wp-image-20375" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-640x303.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-370x175.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-125x59.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-560x265.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-640x303.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="303" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-640x303.jpg" alt="Chinese Egg Noodles From Scratch" class="wp-image-20375" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-640x303.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-370x175.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-125x59.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2-560x265.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Alkaline-Egg-Noodles-1698_2.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>Chinese Egg Noodles From Scratch</figcaption></figure></div><p>I love the feeling of euphoria and pride when I successfully make something from scratch. Kneading soft, malleable dough with my hands for a few minutes? That I can handle. I find the rhythmic motions relaxing. What I don&#8217;t love, is when a recipe is too much of a chore.&nbsp;Pounding an ultra-stiff dough with my fist for even 1 minute while not even making a dent? Too much work.</p><p><strong>That&#8217;s when it&#8217;s time to use a pasta machine</strong> to help retain my love of noodle-making, my children&#8217;s love of noodle-making, and our sanity.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="437" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20437'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cutting ramen dough into strands" class="wp-image-14949" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-640x437.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-125x85.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-370x253.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-560x382.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-640x437.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="437" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-640x437.jpg" alt="Cutting ramen dough into strands" class="wp-image-14949" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-640x437.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-125x85.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-370x253.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790-560x382.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1790.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption> Kids Making Homemade Ramen Noodles From Scratch</figcaption></figure></div> <script async src="//pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script> <ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block; text-align:center;" data-ad-layout="in-article" data-ad-format="fluid" data-ad-client="ca-pub-9502811346572347" data-ad-slot="3259390564"></ins> <script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script> <br> </br><p><strong style="font-size: inherit;">But this ramen dough was just way too tough to knead by hand let alone roll out by hand.</strong><span style="font-size: inherit;">&nbsp;So we used an alternate kneading technique that worked for us in the Chinese egg noodle recipe. We took a large rolling pin and hit the dough hard, turned the dough over, repeat. That helped a little.</span></p><p>What helped a lot was using our pasta machine. We have two of these&nbsp;<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0009U5OSO/ref=as_li_qf_sp_asin_il_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;tag=outandaboindu-20&amp;camp=1789&amp;creative=9325&amp;linkCode=as2&amp;creativeASIN=B0009U5OSO&amp;linkId=b6d4e9b50313424c23ac5de64bca2123" target="_blank"><strong>Italian-made pasta machines from Marcato</strong></a>&nbsp;to make things easier for us. One in our Dubai home and one in my parents&#8217; home for when we visit. I was unsure of it at first but now I can&#8217;t imagine making noodles without it (bonus: it comes in 9 different colors so you can color-coordinate your kitchen.)</p> <script type="text/javascript">amzn_assoc_tracking_id = "outandaboindu-20";
amzn_assoc_ad_mode = "manual";
amzn_assoc_ad_type = "smart";
amzn_assoc_marketplace = "amazon";
amzn_assoc_region = "US";
amzn_assoc_design = "enhanced_links";
amzn_assoc_asins = "B00170EB1Q";
amzn_assoc_placement = "adunit";
amzn_assoc_linkid = "dae875d816fcb78ca3240665d03d2751";</script> <script src="//z-na.amazon-adsystem.com/widgets/onejs?MarketPlace=US"></script> <p>You just feed the dough into the machine and crank the handle to flatten the dough until the desired thinness. And then you cut the flattened dough into thin strands. The machine does all the hard work and this becomes a <strong>no-knead Ramen noodles from scratch recipe</strong>.<br><script src="//z-na.amazon-adsystem.com/widgets/onejs?MarketPlace=US"></p></script></p><div class="content-box-blue"><p>Wondering which pasta machine is best to buy? <a href="/marcato-vs-imperia-pasta-machine/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Click here to read my review of two popular Italian-made brands: the Marcato Atlas versus the Cucina Pro Imperia.</span></a></p></div><hr class="wp-block-separator"/><h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>What are Ramen Noodles?</strong></h2><p>Ramen is a type of Japanese noodle made from wheat flour. In Japan, ramen is eaten freshly made, not like the inexpensive packets of instant noodles (you know, the ones that are 10¢ a packet?) which are deep-fried and full of MSG.</p><p>Ramen originated from China: the term “ramen”&nbsp;may have been derived from the Chinese words for pulled noodles (&#8220;la mian&#8221;) because Chinese noodles were traditionally pulled by hand. Another theory is that &#8220;ramen was derived from Chinese &#8220;lo mien&#8221; which is boiled noodles tossed with sauce.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator"/><h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Can Ramen Noodles Be Made Successfully at Home?</strong></h2><p>Yes!</p><p>You most likely have all the ingredients in your pantry to make homemade ramen noodles from scratch. This is an eggless Japanese ramen noodle recipe and needs only 3 ingredients.</p><p>To make fresh ramen at home, all you need is:</p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>All-purpose flour</li><li>Water</li><li>Alkaline agent: either <strong>lye water</strong> (aka <strong>&#8220;kansui&#8221;</strong> and can be purchased from an Asian grocery store) or <strong>baking soda</strong>.</li></ul><p>To use baking soda to make ramen noodles, you must first <em><strong>bake</strong></em> it in the oven for one hour. <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="/baked-baking-soda-alkaline-noodles/" target="_blank"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Click here for my instructions on how to make *<em>baked*&nbsp;</em>baking soda</span></a> and why alkaline agents are essential to making ramen noodles.</p><p>After you&#8217;ve mastered making ramen noodles from scratch, you can serve it with my <a href="https://gingerandscotch.com/tonkotsu-shoyu-ramen-pressure-cooker/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Tonkotsu ramen with braised pork belly</span></a>.</p><hr class="wp-block-separator"/><h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>How to Make Homemade Ramen Noodles From Scratch</strong></h2><p>Continue reading below for <strong>detailed instructions</strong> (with step-by-step photos) on how to make ramen noodles from scratch or you can <strong><a href="#wprm-recipe-container-15078" data-recipe="15078" style="color: #333333;" class="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal">click here to jump to the print-friendly recipe</a></strong>.</p><p>Enjoy and have fun with this!</p><div class="content-box-yellow"><h3><strong>The basic steps are as follows:</strong></h3><ol><li>Add lye water or <a href="https://gingerandscotch.com/baked-baking-soda-alkaline-noodles" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">baked baking soda</a>&nbsp;to warm water to make an alkaline solution.</li><li>Add alkaline solution to the flour; mix and squish dough into a ball.</li><li>Rest dough 30 minutes.</li><li>&#8220;Knead&#8221; 2-3 minutes with rolling pin.</li><li>Roll dough flat with pasta machine.</li><li>Cut dough into long strips of noodles.</li><li>Simmer noodles briefly in boiling water.</li></ol></div><p><strong>You will need the following (serves 4):</strong></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li>240 grams all-purpose flour (2 cups)</li><li>2 teaspoons baked baking soda (or 1 teaspoon of lye water aka <strong>&#8220;kansui&#8221;</strong>)</li><li>1/2 cup plus 1 teaspoon warm water (you might need more but this is a good start)</li></ul><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0009U5OSO/ref=as_li_qf_sp_asin_il_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;tag=outandaboindu-20&amp;camp=1789&amp;creative=9325&amp;linkCode=as2&amp;creativeASIN=B0009U5OSO&amp;linkId=b6d4e9b50313424c23ac5de64bca2123" target="_blank">Pasta machine</a></li><li>Large mixing bowl</li><li>Spoon or spatula or chopsticks</li><li>Measuring cup or kitchen scale. I prefer a kitchen scale (<a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0020L6T7K/ref=as_li_qf_sp_asin_il_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;tag=outandaboindu-20&amp;camp=1789&amp;creative=9325&amp;linkCode=as2&amp;creativeASIN=B0020L6T7K&amp;linkId=b095bef4b4b12e45a0eb614c7b7bdc41" target="_blank">I have this OXO one</a>) because it makes for more consistent measuring as a cup of flour can range anywhere from 100 grams to 300 grams depending on how lightly or tightly packed the flour is.)</li></ul> <script async src="//pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script> <ins class="adsbygoogle" style="display:block; text-align:center;" data-ad-layout="in-article" data-ad-format="fluid" data-ad-client="ca-pub-9502811346572347" data-ad-slot="3259390564"></ins> <script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script> <br> </br><p></p><hr class="wp-block-separator"/><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 1 — Make an alkaline water solution.</strong></h4><p>Add <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://gingerandscotch.com/baked-baking-soda-alkaline-noodles" target="_blank">baked baking soda</a> (or use &#8220;kansui&#8221; if you have that) to the warm water and mix well to make an alkaline solution.</p><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 2&nbsp;</strong><strong>—&nbsp;</strong><strong>Mix flour and alkaline solution in a large mixing bowl.</strong></h4><p>Place flour in a large bowl and pour in the alkaline solution.</p><p>The flour will immediately turn a yellowish color as the natural yellow pigments in flavonoid compounds that are otherwise colorless at neutral pH are liberated at a higher basic pH of 9-11, giving the noodles a characteristic golden hue (source: <a rel="noopener noreferrer" href="http://luckypeach.com/opusculum-alkaline-ramen-noodles/" target="_blank">Lucky Peach</a>).</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Adding baked baking soda to flour" class="wp-image-14952" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-640x426.jpg" alt="Adding baked baking soda to flour" class="wp-image-14952" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1887.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption> Adding alkaline water turns the mixture yellow</figcaption></figure></div><p>Use a spoon, spatula or chopsticks to mix in the water. The flour will become a crumbly texture and that is what you want for now.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="330" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20330'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14958" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-640x330.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-125x65.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-370x191.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage.jpg 800w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-560x289.jpg 560w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-640x330.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="330" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-640x330.jpg" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14958" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-640x330.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-125x65.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-370x191.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage.jpg 800w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline-Dough-collage-560x289.jpg 560w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>Mix with spoon or chopsticks until the water is incorporated into the flour</figcaption></figure></div><p>Use your hands to squish the flour crumbs together into a ball.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14955" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-640x426.jpg" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14955" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1898.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>Use your hands and squeeze flour &#8220;crumbs&#8221; into a ball</figcaption></figure></div><p> If the flour doesn&#8217;t completely form a ball after a bit of squeezing, then add more water, <strong>but only a tablespoon at a time</strong>, until you get one cohesive ball.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14956" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-640x426.jpg" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14956" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1900.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>If all the flour doesn&#8217;t come together into ball, add a little more water</figcaption></figure></div><p>This is what you are aiming for &#8211; a dry and crumbly looking dough with barely any crumbs left in the mixing bowl:</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14957" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-640x426.jpg" alt="Mixing flour and alkaline water" class="wp-image-14957" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1913.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption> See how all the flour has come together into a ball with no more &#8220;crumbs&#8221; in the bowl?</figcaption></figure></div><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 3&nbsp;— Rest dough for 30 minutes at room temperature.</strong></h4><p>Wrap the dough in plastic wrap or place it in a bowl covered with a damp towel so the dough does not dry out.</p><p>Allow the dough to rest for 30 minutes at room temperaure (just enough time for the kids and I to watch one episode of our favorite Netflix show &#8211; currently Voltron because it is the <em>coolest reboot EVER</em>!).</p><p>You can also rest the dough in the fridge overnight if you don&#8217;t plan on rolling the dough out right away.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Resting Ramen Dough" class="wp-image-14938" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-640x426.jpg" alt="Resting Ramen Dough" class="wp-image-14938" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1929.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption> Rest dough by covering with a damp cloth (instead of plastic wrap to decrease plastic waste)</figcaption></figure></div><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 4&nbsp;— &#8220;Knead&#8221; the dough for 2 to 3 minutes.</strong></h4><p>This is not a soft, smooth and easy dough to knead like the <a href="https://gingerandscotch.com/simple-homemade-chinese-wheat-noodles/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">basic Chinese noodle dough</a>&nbsp;or the <a href="https://gingerandscotch.com/homemade-chinese-egg-noodles-from-scratch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chinese egg noodle dough</a> we previously made. The kids and I really struggled kneading by hand so I let them use a large rolling pin to beat the dough like they did in the Chinese egg noodle recipe.</p><p>They took turns beating the dough for about 3 minutes. To &#8220;knead&#8221; with a rolling pin, give the dough a couple of whacks, pat into a ball, whack it again and repeat. &nbsp;I find that putting on their favorite music helps the time pass quickly. We&#8217;re currently rocking to <em>&#8220;Shake it Off&#8221;</em> from the silly kids movie Sing.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20400%20553'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Having fun with ramen dough" class="wp-image-14940" width="400" height="553" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1599-90x125.jpg 90w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1599-216x300.jpg 216w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1599-640x890.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1599-640x890.jpg" alt="Having fun with ramen dough" class="wp-image-14940" width="400" height="553" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1599-90x125.jpg 90w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1599-216x300.jpg 216w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /></noscript><figcaption> Kids kneading dough by beating it with a rolling pin[/caption]</figcaption></figure></div><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 5&nbsp;</strong><strong>— </strong><strong>Roll the dough flat with a pasta machine.</strong></h4><p>Set your pasta machine to the widest setting (Level 0 for <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0009U5OSO/ref=as_li_qf_sp_asin_il_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;tag=outandaboindu-20&amp;camp=1789&amp;creative=9325&amp;linkCode=as2&amp;creativeASIN=B0009U5OSO&amp;linkId=b6d4e9b50313424c23ac5de64bca2123" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Marcato brand</a> and Level 6 for <a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B0001IXA0I/ref=as_li_qf_sp_asin_il_tl?ie=UTF8&amp;tag=outandaboindu-20&amp;camp=1789&amp;creative=9325&amp;linkCode=as2&amp;creativeASIN=B0001IXA0I&amp;linkId=f123052ed52de98dc2d8f4325f92718b" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Imperia brand</a>). Divide your dough in half and return the unused portion to it&#8217;s plastic wrap or towel covered bowl.</p><p>Flatten the other half of your dough as much as possible by hand (or whack with the rolling pin again) and start feeding it through the pasta machine.</p><p>Don&#8217;t be discouraged by the first pass of the dough through the pasta machine. It will look pretty raggedy and holey and uneven but will become smooth and even after a few more passes.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20399%20599'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="First pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14941" width="399" height="599" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-640x960.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-83x125.jpg 83w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-200x300.jpg 200w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-400x600.jpg 400w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-560x840.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 399px) 100vw, 399px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-640x960.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-640x960.jpg" alt="First pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14941" width="399" height="599" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-640x960.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-83x125.jpg 83w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-200x300.jpg 200w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-400x600.jpg 400w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617-560x840.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1617.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 399px) 100vw, 399px" /></noscript><figcaption> First pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine[/caption]</figcaption></figure></div><p>Fold the raggedy dough into thirds and pass it through the machine again. Repeat 3 or 4 more times.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20401%20541'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="First pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14942" width="401" height="541" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-92x125.jpg 92w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-222x300.jpg 222w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-560x757.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 401px) 100vw, 401px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-640x866.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-640x866.jpg" alt="First pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14942" width="401" height="541" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-92x125.jpg 92w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-222x300.jpg 222w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629-560x757.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1629.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 401px) 100vw, 401px" /></noscript><figcaption> Fold Dough into thirds</figcaption></figure></div><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter is-resized"><img decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20400%20266'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="2nd pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14943" width="400" height="266" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-640x426.jpg" alt="2nd pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14943" width="400" height="266" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1632.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /></noscript><figcaption> Pass dough through pasta machine[/caption]</figcaption></figure></div><p> After a few passes through the machine, it will look and feel smooth and become more and more rectangular. The machine is essentially kneading the dough for you.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="431" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20431'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="2nd pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14944" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-640x431.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-125x84.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-370x249.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-560x377.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-640x431.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="431" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-640x431.jpg" alt="2nd pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14944" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-640x431.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-125x84.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-370x249.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644-560x377.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1644.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>After the 2nd pass though (level 0)</figcaption></figure></div><p><strong>Only fold the dough into thirds</strong> when you are passing it through <strong><em>the widest setting</em></strong> of the machine.</p><p>Keep folding in thirds and passing it through the widest setting until you get one long rectangular piece that&#8217;s not broken into pieces (it took us 6-8 passes).</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="442" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20442'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Second pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14945" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-640x442.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-125x86.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-370x256.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-560x387.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-640x442.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="442" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-640x442.jpg" alt="Second pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14945" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-640x442.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-125x86.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-370x256.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654-560x387.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1654.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>Fold Dough into thirds</figcaption></figure></div><p> Once the dough is flattened to a nice looking (not holey or broken into bits) rectangular shape, pass the dough through the machine two more times but&nbsp;<strong>in one piece without folding it into thirds</strong>. You are still using the widest setting of the machine.</p><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 6&nbsp;</strong><strong>— </strong><strong>Continue rolling the dough through the pasta maker until desired thinness.</strong></h4><p>Now adjust the machine setting to the next size setting and pass the dough through 2 times but remember:&nbsp;<strong>DO NOT FOLD in thirds anymore</strong>. Pass the dough through as a single sheet. &nbsp;Dust with a little bit of tapioca or corn starch before each pass to prevent any possible stick-age.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Third pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14947" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-640x426.jpg" alt="Third pass of ramen dough through the pasta machine" class="wp-image-14947" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1714.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>Keep passing dough through the machine</figcaption></figure></div><p> With the Marcato pasta machine, we started with the widest setting of 0, then went to level 1, then level 2, then level 3 and stopped at level 4 which according to the user manual is 1.9mm (1/16 inch). We did try level 5 but the noodles came out too thin for our liking.</p><p>At this point, the dough will not be completely smooth like the <a href="https://gingerandscotch.com/homemade-udon-noodles-from-scratch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">our homemade udon dough</a> but once it passes through the cutters, it will be still become beautiful noodles!</p><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 7&nbsp;</strong><strong>— </strong><strong>Cut dough into long strips of noodles with the pasta machine.</strong></h4><p>Finally we are ready to cut the dough into strands! Our Marcato pasta machine came with two size options &#8211; a thick fettucine size or a thin spaghettini size. We used the spaghettini cutter to make these ramen noodles.</p><p>Our flattened dough was a bit long so the children cut it in half using a dough scraper/cutter or you can also use a knife.</p><p>Lightly dust the dough with tapioca or corn starch and then pass it through the cutters:</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="826" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20826'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cutting ramen dough into strands" class="wp-image-14961" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-640x826.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-97x125.jpg 97w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-232x300.jpg 232w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-560x723.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-640x826.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="826" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-640x826.jpg" alt="Cutting ramen dough into strands" class="wp-image-14961" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-640x826.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-97x125.jpg 97w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-232x300.jpg 232w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802-560x723.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1802.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption> Voila! Noodles!</figcaption></figure></div><p> This is our favorite part &#8211; watching that piece of dough slowly emerge out of the machine as many individual strands of noodles! It&#8217;s a <em><span style="color: #ff0000;"><strong>WOW</strong> </span></em>moment for us every time.</p><p>Repeat the process with the other half of the dough.</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="762" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20762'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Cutting ramen dough into strands" class="wp-image-14959" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-640x762.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-105x125.jpg 105w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-252x300.jpg 252w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-560x667.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-640x762.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="762" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-640x762.jpg" alt="Cutting ramen dough into strands" class="wp-image-14959" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-640x762.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-105x125.jpg 105w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-252x300.jpg 252w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806-560x667.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1806.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript><figcaption>Kids Making Homemade Ramen Noodles From Scratch</figcaption></figure></div><h4 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Step 8&nbsp;— Simmer noodles in boiling water.</strong></h4><p>To cook these noodles, bring a large pot of water to boil. Then add the noodles and cook for 1 minute. These noodles are thin so don&#8217;t need much time to cook at all or they&#8217;ll become very gummy/sticky. You want to undercook them slightly as they&#8217;ll also soften up slightly in your soup broth. Drain and rinse under cold water.</p><p>There you go &#8211; fresh homemade ramen noodles from scratch the no-knead easy way!</p><div class="wp-block-image"><figure class="aligncenter"><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20640%20426'%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Homemade fresh ramen noodles from scratch (Alkaline Noodles)" class="wp-image-14950" data-lazy-srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865.jpg 800w" data-lazy-sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" data-lazy-src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-640x426.jpg" /><noscript><img decoding="async" width="640" height="426" src="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-640x426.jpg" alt="Homemade fresh ramen noodles from scratch (Alkaline Noodles)" class="wp-image-14950" srcset="https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-640x426.jpg 640w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-125x83.jpg 125w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-370x247.jpg 370w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865-560x373.jpg 560w, https://gingerandscotch.com/wp_sd/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/Alkaline_Noodles-1865.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></noscript></figure></div><p>When you make your first batch of noodles, you will feel as proud and as euphoric as we did. Don&#8217;t worry if your first batch isn&#8217;t perfect. <strong>Remember: Noodles aren&#8217;t meant to be perfect, they&#8217;re meant to be shared.</strong></p><p>After you&#8217;ve mastered making ramen noodles from scratch, you can serve it with my <a rel="noreferrer noopener" href="https://gingerandscotch.com/tonkotsu-shoyu-ramen-pressure-cooker/" target="_blank"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Tonkotsu ramen with braised pork belly</span></a>.</p><p>Be sure to tag us on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/gingerandscotch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a> (@gingerandscotch) and <a href="https://twitter.com/GingerAndScotch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Twitter</a> (@gingerandscotch) and show us your noodle-making in action.</p><p>Happy Noodling!<br>-Sandy</p> <script type="text/javascript">amzn_assoc_placement = "adunit0";
amzn_assoc_search_bar = "true";
amzn_assoc_tracking_id = "outandaboindu-20";
amzn_assoc_ad_mode = "manual";
amzn_assoc_ad_type = "smart";
amzn_assoc_marketplace = "amazon";
amzn_assoc_region = "US";
amzn_assoc_title = "My Amazon Picks";
amzn_assoc_linkid = "97ef0eeda435c8303b4646b112bfa840";
